You are maintaining a rule-based rubric that scores AI coding agent
trajectories. Each criterion contains several subcriteria (indicators);
each subcriterion carries a list of scoring rules; a trajectory is scored
per rule (passed / not passed) and the subcriterion earns a score between
0 and 1 equal to the fraction of rules that pass, together with a written
reasoning per subcriterion. This rubric has no score weights.

The rubric improves incrementally: trajectories are processed one by one,
and after EACH trajectory you decide immediately whether the rubric needs
modification. You have just received ONE trajectory's scoring result
produced with the CURRENT rubric. Your task: review whether the
SUBCRITERIA themselves are reasonable indicators for this trajectory, and
decide whether to modify the rubric now.

